<http://example.org/artifact-capability-shapes> dcterms:identifier "artifact_capability" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/oemethod> ;
    rdfs:comment "SHACL role of the artifact-capability vocabulary. Both classes represent open enumeration schemes whose concrete level taxonomy (e.g. Nascent/Developing/Mature, or a numeric score) is not yet decided (L-110: minting it now, on the evidence of zero producers, would encode incidental choices as though settled). Lightweight nodeKind coverage is real, permanent shape coverage — not a placeholder for later semantic constraints, since there is nothing skeleton-shaped about the classes themselves.",
        "v1.1.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): every named subject now carries dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/artifact-capability-shapes> (its module), the first step of the consolidation of this package's files into one file per role. No term, label or definition changed."@en ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/artifact-capability-shapes/1.0.0> ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/artifact-capability-shapes/1.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.1.0" .

