<http://example.org/oemethod> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-06T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:creator oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor,
        "the method author" ;
    dcterms:description "The SHACL shapes of the OE Method's domain vocabularies as ONE file (BP-D54). Each former suite is a module; every shape says dcterms:isPartOf <its module>. The twelve generated shape files left the package at this step (reproducible with the shape-derivation tool). A pure union of the hand-written suites, proved."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "oemethod" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-07T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime,
        "2026-10-11T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:publisher oe-prov:Org_IKU_Department_of_ComputerEngineering ;
    dcterms:rights "Copyright (c) 2025-2026 a university & the method author. Licensed under CC BY 4.0." ;
    dcterms:rightsHolder oe-prov:Org_IKU_Department_of_ComputerEngineering ;
    dcterms:title "OE Method — SHACL shapes (one file for the package)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The SHACL shapes of the OE Method's domain vocabularies as ONE file (BP-D54). Each former suite is a module; every shape says dcterms:isPartOf <its module>. The twelve generated shape files left the package at this step (reproducible with the shape-derivation tool). A pure union of the hand-written suites, proved."@en ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/oemethod/1.0.0>,
        <http://example.org/oemethod/1.1.0>,
        <http://example.org/oemethod/1.1.1> ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/oemethod/1.2.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.2.0" ;
    skos:changeNote "v1.1.0 (2026-10-06): re-derived after the governing pack told the closed QualityAssessment shape of the measurement module about artifact-capability:hasCapabilityLevel and artifact-capability:hasScoreBasis, so a capability assessment can record its level and the measured values behind it on the record itself. No shape gained or lost a constraint, and only that module changed."@en,
        "v1.1.1 (2026-10-07, PATCH): 117 identical copies of anonymous constraints in 47 shapes (redo and reliability modules) are removed, derived from the pack's repair; a union of two files had kept both. No shape added or removed, no constraint changed."@en,
        "v1.2.0 (2026-10-11): re-derived after the governing package changed 3 module(s): http://example.org/measurement, http://example.org/redo, http://example.org/reliability. Nothing else changed."@en .

