<http://example.org/redo> rdfs:label "a reliability ontology SHACL Shapes v2.0.6"@en ;
    dcterms:created "2026-02-24T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description """Machine-executable SHACL shapes implementing the a reliability ontology v2 
verification pipeline. These shapes catch both TBox (class-level) and ABox 
(individual-level) quality defects, including mechanical labels, tautological 
definitions, property asymmetry across namespaces, and undeclared types. 
Run with any SHACL-compliant validator."""@en,
        "v2.0.6: Rewrote C8V_FormatCheckShape (FILTER NOT EXISTS{FILTER} → FILTER(!REGEX())) and C6PROVOManifestShape (FILTER NOT EXISTS{FILTER} → OPTIONAL{FILTER}+FILTER(!BOUND())) for pySHACL compatibility. Neither MINUS nor nested FILTER in FILTER NOT EXISTS is supported in SHACL-AF SPARQL constraints."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "redo" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/oemethod> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-04-10T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime,
        "2026-10-06T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime,
        "2026-10-07T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment "SHACL validation shapes for the a reliability ontology Reliability Engineering Domain Ontology v2.5.x. Validates documentation quality, annotation coverage, naming conventions, and PROV-O coupling."@en,
        "redo v4.3.1 (2026-10-07, PATCH): 45 shapes that this suite holds in common with another suite each carried every one of their anonymous constraints twice, identical copies left by merging two files (a union does not drop a blank node). One copy of each is kept; no shape added or removed, no constraint changed."@en,
        "redo_shacl v4.0.0 — CONSOLIDATED single-file suite. Merges the full v3.0.0 C1-C8 gate (48 shapes, C2 skos:definition at Violation) + the coverage/measurement add-ons (S-COV-2 dcterms:source, S-COV-3 individual source, S-MEAS-2 score-metric). Supersedes and replaces v2_0_13_3, v3_0_0, v3_1_0, v3_2_0 (all retired). C2 stays Violation per BP-D24/L-66 (the v3.1/v3.2 Warning-level S-COV-1 was dropped as redundant-and-weaker). Authored 2026-05-28."@en,
        "v2.0.13.1 — I-05 remediation. Updates C7+ TypeDeclarationShape SPARQL to dynamically read owl:imports declarations from the focus graph, suppressing false-positive Violations on classes that ARE declared in imported (but not currently merged) vocabularies. Standalone-vs-imports-merged validation now produces the same C7+ results in both modes (when imports are declared in the focus graph)."@en,
        "v2.0.7 adds four structural validation shapes (S-STRUCT-1 to S-STRUCT-4) covering graph-structural pathologies invisible to annotation-only validation: (1) named OWL restrictions used as subClassOf parents, (2) isolated classes with no hierarchy placement, (3) multiple inheritance from disjoint parents (logical unsatisfiability), (4) cycles in rdfs:subClassOf chains. These shapes use SPARQL property paths and require pySHACL ≥ 0.6.0 with SPARQL 1.1 property path support. Note: S-STRUCT-4 (cycle detection) uses rdfs:subClassOf+ — confirmed working in pySHACL via runtime empirical test 2026-04-10."@en,
        "v2.0.8: S-STRUCT-1 tightened with FILTER(isIRI(?restrictionParent)) to prevent false positives on legitimate blank-node OWL restrictions (someValuesFrom, allValuesFrom)."@en,
        "v2.0.9 (2026-05-01): CRITICAL fix to S-STRUCT-4. Prior `rdfs:subClassOf+ $this` SPARQL fired 343 false positives under pyshacl `inference='rdfs'` because RDFS reflexive entailment adds `?C rdfs:subClassOf ?C` for every owl:Class. The 2026-04-10 'runtime empirical test' that supposedly confirmed working behaviour did not exercise the rdfs-inference operating profile. Fix: require a non-reflexive intermediate step (`?intermediate != $this`). This is the canonical RDFS-safe cycle-detection pattern. Verified 2026-05-01: 0 violations on redo_v2_5_11.ttl; preserves true cycle detection (synthetic cycle test still fires)."@en,
        "v4.2.0 (2026-10-05): the nine property declarations (the same nine declared in reliability_tbox v7.14.0) were removed from this file, so it holds shapes only (BP-D53). Their declaration lives in the reliability T-Box; no triple was lost from the corpus."@en,
        "v4.3.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): every named subject now carries dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/redo> (its module), the first step of the consolidation of this package's files into one file per role. No term, label or definition changed."@en ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/redo-shacl/3.0.0>,
        <http://example.org/redo-shacl/4.2.0>,
        <http://example.org/redo-shacl/4.3.0>,
        <http://example.org/redo/2.0.13> ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/redo-shacl/4.3.1> ;
    owl:versionInfo "4.3.1" .

