    dcterms:modified "2026-10-07T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:publisher oe-prov:Org_IKU_Department_of_ComputerEngineering ;
    dcterms:rights "Copyright (c) 2025-2026 a university & the method author. Licensed under CC BY 4.0."@en ;
    dcterms:rightsHolder oe-prov:Org_IKU_Department_of_ComputerEngineering ;
    rdfs:comment "membership for the subjects v20.99.0 missed: its tool skipped every IRI below the header IRI, taking it for a version IRI (66 quality individuals under .../quality/sparql-impl-v1.0.0#, one shape under .../drift18#)"@en,
        "reliability PATCH v7.0.1. Sprint F1 ghost-reference cleanup: 0 dangling class references redirected to canonical homes; 0 dangling subClassOf claims dropped per L-47 (cross-subject methodological-vs-subsumption discipline). Per BP-D4/D5 gates: HermiT PASS, SHACL no new violations."@en,
        "reliability SHACL v5.1.0 (version-aligned)"@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.4.0 (version-aligned)"@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.5.0 (MINOR) — 55 mitigates shape demoted to sh:Warning per L-20."@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.6.0 (MINOR) — version aligned; v17.23.0 L' demotions applied across all reliability shape-bearing files."@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.7.0 (MINOR) per v17.29.0 industrial-hardening item #4: retired stale broad C7+ shape (http://example.org/redo#C7plus_TypeDeclarationShape) which was superseded but not removed when strict/advisory split was introduced. Extended STRICT + ADVISORY allowlists with: http://example.org/redo#, http://example.org/redo-c7-split#, http://example.org/oe-prov#, http://example.org/measurement# (typo fix from \"oee-measurement\"). Result: reliability standalone moves from 14V/76W to 0V/<76W (target — empirically verified)."@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.7.1 (PATCH) per v17.30.0 — operationalized 2 CQs via SHACL-shape-graph SPARQL queries."@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.8.0 (MINOR) per v17.32.0 Option B — added 274 auto-generated skeleton NodeShapes for owl:Class declarations lacking SHACL coverage. Per BP-D27 each skeleton carries kb:isSkeletonShape true. Mechanical Roadmap Step 1; semantic constraints in Step 2."@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.9.0 (MINOR) per Option C — 274 skeletons upgraded: 75 full-semantic + 199 lightweight per BP-D30."@en,
        "reliability SHACL v7.9.1 (PATCH) per v18.0.0 — removed \"web-page-construction\" from C7plus_strict_TypeDeclarationShape whitelist comment."@en,
        "reliability shacl v7.1.0 (version-aligned to TBox)"@en,
        "reliability shacl v7.3.0 (version-aligned to TBox)"@en,
        "reliability v4.0.0 (MAJOR from v3.1.0): removed all owl:equivalentClass axioms (20 total in TBox). Per user rule 2026-05-14 'use the ORIGINAL class.' Deleted 19 duplicate class declarations (18 quality-dimension duplicates of OQC + reliability:SeverityLevel duplicate of core). Converted reliability:Postmortem ≡ kb:RetrospectiveMeeting to rdfs:subClassOf per BP-D19 (related-but-distinct: Postmortem is a failure-focused specialization of RetrospectiveMeeting). Consumers using reliability:Reliability etc. should migrate to quality:Reliability."@en,
        "reliability v8.3.1 (2026-10-07, PATCH): 47 shapes that this suite holds in common with another suite each carried every one of their anonymous constraints twice, identical copies left by merging two files (a union does not drop a blank node). One copy of each is kept; no shape added or removed, no constraint changed."@en,
        "reliability_shacl v7.6.1 (PATCH) per v17.24.0 Option M — added quality:hasSPARQLImplementation to 1 operationalizable CQs and NOT-OPERATIONALIZABLE annotations to 2 descriptive CQs. Additive annotations only."@en,
        "reliability_shacl v7.6.2 (PATCH) per v17.28.0 industrial-hardening — added CC BY 4.0 license, copyright, publisher/rightsHolder (IKÜ Computer Engineering), PROV-O wasGeneratedBy + wasAttributedTo (the method author). Additive ontology metadata only — no semantic changes."@en,
        "v8.1.0 (2026-10-05): the nine property declarations moved to reliability_tbox v7.14.0 and the three competency-question individuals to reliability_abox v7.9.0, so this file holds shapes only (BP-D53). No triple was added or removed; only the file they sit in changed."@en,
        "v8.2.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): every named subject now carries dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> (its module), the first step of the consolidation of this package's files into one file per role. No term, label or definition changed."@en ;
